1
00:00:00,709 --> 00:00:02,795
OKAY, GREAT. BYE.

2
00:00:02,795 --> 00:00:05,088
HEY. SO, GUESS
WHO'S COMING TO
THANKSGIVING DINNER?

3
00:00:05,088 --> 00:00:06,423
SIDNEY POITIER.

4
00:00:06,423 --> 00:00:07,675
( laughing )

5
00:00:07,675 --> 00:00:10,594
I MISS RACHEL.

6
00:00:10,594 --> 00:00:12,387
NO, MY PARENTS.
OH, THAT'S GREAT.

7
00:00:12,387 --> 00:00:14,515
THEY HAVEN'T SEEN
THE PLACE SINCE
I MOVED IN.

8
00:00:14,515 --> 00:00:16,642
YEAH, AND YOU KNOW
IF YOU COULD NOT
MENTION TO THEM

9
00:00:16,642 --> 00:00:18,519
THAT WE LIVE TOGETHER,
THAT WOULD BE GREAT.

10
00:00:18,519 --> 00:00:21,229
I WAS THINKING
WE'D EAT AROUND 4:00.

11
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,690
WHY CAN'T I TELL THEM
THAT WE LIVE TOGETHER?

12
00:00:22,690 --> 00:00:24,065
BECAUSE THEY DON'T KNOW
WE'RE DATING.

13
00:00:24,065 --> 00:00:26,819
DO YOU THINK
WE SHOULD EAT
IN THE KITCHEN?

14
00:00:26,819 --> 00:00:28,278
WHY HAVEN'T YOU TOLD THEM?

15
00:00:28,278 --> 00:00:30,990
UM, WELL, I WAS GOING TO,
I WAS REALLY WAS

16
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:34,618
BUT, UM, THEN, SOMEWHERE,
JUST OUT OF NOWHERE, I DIDN'T.

17
00:00:34,618 --> 00:00:36,411
WHY HAVEN'T
YOU TOLD THEM?

18
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:38,038
WOULDN'T THEY
BE HAPPY?

19
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:39,832
SO DINNER IN THE KITCHEN
AROUND 4:00.

20
00:00:39,832 --> 00:00:41,166
I'LL SEE YOU THEN.

21
00:00:41,166 --> 00:00:43,335
WHY WOULDN'T THEY BE HAPPY?

22
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,337
WELL, UH, BECAUSE...

23
00:00:45,337 --> 00:00:48,298
MAINLY, UH...

24
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:49,257
THEY DON'T LIKE YOU.

25
00:00:50,342 --> 00:00:51,343
I'M SORRY.

26
00:00:51,343 --> 00:00:53,012
WHAT? WHAT? WHY?

27
00:00:53,012 --> 00:00:55,681
MAYBE BECAUSE YOU USED
TO BE ALOOF, OR THAT YOU'RE

28
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:57,599
REALLY SARCASTIC,
OR THAT, YOU KNOW

29
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:58,851
YOU JOKE AROUND ALL THE TIME

30
00:00:58,851 --> 00:01:00,143
OR THAT YOU TAKE OFF
YOUR CLOTHES

31
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,021
AND YOU THROW THEM ON THE COUCH.

32
00:01:02,021 --> 00:01:04,690
IS THIS WHY THEY DON'T LIKE ME
OR WHY YOU DON'T LIKE ME?

33
00:01:04,690 --> 00:01:07,275
LOOK, I KNOW THAT I
SHOULD HAVE TOLD THEM.

34
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:10,529
I KNOW I SHOULDN'T CARE
WHAT THEY THINK. I'M SORRY.

35
00:01:10,529 --> 00:01:12,698
YOU KNOW WHAT?
IT'LL BE OKAY, IT'LL BE OKAY

36
00:01:12,698 --> 00:01:15,325
BECAUSE WHEN THEY COME OVER,
I WILL BE ALL CHARMING.

37
00:01:15,325 --> 00:01:17,202
I WILL MAKE THEM
FALL IN LOVE WITH ME

38
00:01:17,202 --> 00:01:18,704
AND THEN WE'LL TELL THEM.

39
00:01:18,704 --> 00:01:19,997
YOU REALLY THINK THAT'LL WORK?

40
00:01:19,997 --> 00:01:21,916
HEY, I CAN BE
PRETTY CHARMING, BABE.

41
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:23,584
WON YOU OVER, DIDN'T I?

42
00:01:23,584 --> 00:01:26,587
I DON'T THINK YOU'LL EVER GET
MY PARENTS THAT DRUNK.

43
00:01:34,970 --> 00:01:39,307
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

44
00:01:39,307 --> 00:01:41,560
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

45
00:01:41,560 --> 00:01:43,812
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

46
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:47,733
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

47
00:01:47,733 --> 00:01:51,070
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

48
00:01:51,070 --> 00:01:53,280
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

49
00:01:53,280 --> 00:01:57,576
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

50
00:01:57,576 --> 00:02:00,829
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

51
00:02:07,586 --> 00:02:10,089
HEY. OH, GOOD.
ROSS,

52
00:02:10,089 --> 00:02:11,673
YOUR PARENTS
LIKE ME, RIGHT?

53
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:13,592
YES, OF COURSE
THEY LIKE YOU.

54
00:02:13,592 --> 00:02:15,218
WELL, MONICA JUST TOLD ME
THAT THEY DON'T.

55
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:17,054
YEAH, THEY DON'T LIKE YOU.

56
00:02:17,054 --> 00:02:19,264
DO YOU KNOW WHY?

57
00:02:19,264 --> 00:02:21,600
I DON'T KNOW. MAYBE IT'S 'CAUSE
YOU'RE REALLY SARCASTIC

58
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,435
OR, I DON'T KNOW,
MAYBE IT'S 'CAUSE...

59
00:02:23,435 --> 00:02:24,561
WELL, IF PEOPLE DON'T KNOW

60
00:02:24,561 --> 00:02:27,522
THEY SHOULDN'T
JUST GUESS.

61
00:02:27,522 --> 00:02:28,774
THIS IS GREAT.
ANOTHER THANKSGIVING

62
00:02:28,774 --> 00:02:30,442
WITH NOTHING
TO GIVE THANKS FOR.

63
00:02:30,442 --> 00:02:34,113
MAYBE I GIVE THANKS FOR
YOU SHUTTING UP, HUH?

64
00:02:34,113 --> 00:02:35,739
MAYBE I GIVE THANKS

65
00:02:35,739 --> 00:02:37,950
BY TAKING MY PLAYSTATION
OVER TO MY NEW APARTMENT.

66
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:39,118
WELL, MAYBE I LOVE YOU.

67
00:02:39,118 --> 00:02:40,744
( sarcastic mimicking )

68
00:02:40,744 --> 00:02:41,870
HI.
HI.

69
00:02:41,870 --> 00:02:43,413
HEY, GUYS.

70
00:02:43,413 --> 00:02:47,668
NO, I DON'T WANT TO
PLAY VIDEO GAMES, JOE.

71
00:02:50,045 --> 00:02:53,172
ARE YOU GUYS GOING TO CHANDLER'S
FOR THANKSGIVING?

72
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,341
YEAH, YEAH, WHY?
WHAT'S UP?

73
00:02:54,341 --> 00:02:55,843
WELL, ME AND MY DANCER FRIENDS

74
00:02:55,843 --> 00:02:57,511
ARE THINKING
OF DOING THANKSGIVING UPTOWN.

75
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:59,096
I THOUGHT YOU GUYS
MIGHT LIKE TO COME.

76
00:02:59,096 --> 00:03:01,723
FOR REAL?

77
00:03:01,723 --> 00:03:03,058
YOU SHOULD GO TO CHANDLER'S

78
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:04,685
BECAUSE NONE OF US
KNOWS HOW TO COOK.

79
00:03:04,685 --> 00:03:06,478
WE'LL PROBABLY JUST END UP
DRINKING ALL DAY.

80
00:03:06,478 --> 00:03:10,189
YEAH.
WE GO TO YOURS, YEAH.

81
00:03:10,189 --> 00:03:12,943
YEAH. SEE, WE HAVE TO
STOP ACROSS THE HALL

82
00:03:12,943 --> 00:03:15,529
'CAUSE IT'S MY SISTER,
BUT YOU KNOW, ACTUALLY

83
00:03:15,529 --> 00:03:17,823
GROWING UP
WITH A SISTER WAS NICE

84
00:03:17,823 --> 00:03:20,199
BECAUSE IT REALLY HELPED ME
UNDERSTAND WOMEN.

85
00:03:20,199 --> 00:03:23,162
YOU SHOULD TELL
YOUR FRIENDS THAT.

86
00:03:23,162 --> 00:03:24,913
OKAY.

87
00:03:28,709 --> 00:03:32,420
HOW YOU GOT THREE WOMEN
TO MARRY YOU, I'LL NEVER KNOW.

88
00:03:37,592 --> 00:03:39,094
HEY.

89
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:40,637
HEY, PHEEBS, CHECK IT OUT.

90
00:03:40,637 --> 00:03:42,139
YEAH.
FOR MY DESSERT

91
00:03:42,139 --> 00:03:45,308
I HAVE CHOSEN TO MAKE
A TRADITIONAL ENGLISH TRIFLE.

92
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,310
WOW, THAT SOUNDS GREAT.

93
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:49,354
AND WHAT ARE YOU MAKING, MONICA,
YOU KNOW

94
00:03:49,354 --> 00:03:52,149
IN CASE RACHEL'S DESSERT
IS SO GOOD THAT I EAT ALL OF IT.

95
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:57,487
THERE'S NONE LEFT
FOR ANYBODY ELSE.

96
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:58,864
NOTHING.

97
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:00,365
NOTHING?

98
00:04:00,365 --> 00:04:03,118
YEAH, SWEETIE,
I TRUST YOU.

99
00:04:03,118 --> 00:04:06,663
SO IF I MESS THIS UP, THERE'S
NOTHING ELSE FOR DESSERT?

100
00:04:06,663 --> 00:04:09,166
YOU'RE NOT GOING TO MESS IT UP.

101
00:04:09,166 --> 00:04:10,834
WOW, MONICA, I LOVE THAT.

102
00:04:10,834 --> 00:04:12,836
YOU REALLY HAVE FAITH IN ME.
THANK YOU.

103
00:04:12,836 --> 00:04:14,171
TECHNICAL QUESTION.

104
00:04:14,171 --> 00:04:16,339
HOW DO YOU KNOW
WHEN THE BUTTER IS DONE?

105
00:04:16,339 --> 00:04:19,218
WELL, IT'S DONE ABOUT
TWO MINUTES BEFORE
IT LOOKS THAT.

106
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,513
HEY.
HEY.

107
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:26,100
OH, THE FOOD
SMELLS GREAT, MON.

108
00:04:26,100 --> 00:04:29,352
YEAH, AND THE PLACE
LOOKS SO NICE.

109
00:04:29,352 --> 00:04:30,938
HEY, HAPPY THANKSGIVING,
EVERYBODY.

110
00:04:30,938 --> 00:04:32,064
HAPPY THANKSGIVING.

111
00:04:32,064 --> 00:04:34,066
All:
HAPPY THANKSGIVING.

112
00:04:34,066 --> 00:04:35,650
WELL, THIS HAS BEEN GREAT.

113
00:04:35,650 --> 00:04:36,985
SEE YA.

114
00:04:36,985 --> 00:04:38,112
WHOA, WHOA, WHOA.

115
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:41,990
WHERE ARE YOU GOING?
OH, WE DID SAY

116
00:04:41,990 --> 00:04:45,660
WE'D STOP BY THIS
LITTLE THING JOEY'S
ROOMMATE IS HAVING.

117
00:04:45,660 --> 00:04:48,288
OH, JANINE, THE REALLY
HOT DANCER GIRL?

118
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:52,333
SOME WOULD SAY
SHE'S ATTRACTIVE, YES.

119
00:04:52,333 --> 00:04:54,502
AND WHO ELSE
IS GOING TO BE THERE?

120
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:55,712
SOME OF HER FRIENDS.

121
00:04:55,712 --> 00:04:57,005
HER DANCER FRIENDS?

122
00:04:57,005 --> 00:04:58,632
YES, ALL RIGHT?

123
00:04:58,632 --> 00:05:01,802
ALL OF HER HOT DANCER FRIENDS
ARE GOING TO BE THERE

124
00:05:01,802 --> 00:05:03,971
AND THEY'LL BE DRINKING
AND DANCING

125
00:05:03,971 --> 00:05:05,722
AND WE REALLY WANT TO GO.

126
00:05:07,724 --> 00:05:10,227
DUDE, WE WERE GOOD.

127
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:12,395
YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO GO ANYWHERE.

128
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:14,815
YOU SAID YOU WERE GOING
TO EAT HERE AND YOU'RE
GOING TO EAT HERE.

129
00:05:14,815 --> 00:05:17,901
AND LEAVING US
TO GO SEE HOT DANCER GIRLS

130
00:05:17,901 --> 00:05:19,945
IS NOT VERY THANKSGIVING-Y.

131
00:05:19,945 --> 00:05:21,238
OH, BUT IT IS.

132
00:05:21,238 --> 00:05:23,323
IT'S JUST LIKE
THE FIRST THANKSGIVING

133
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,534
WHEN THE INDIANS
AND THE PILGRIMS
SAT DOWN TO DINNER.

134
00:05:26,534 --> 00:05:29,121
YEAH, YEAH, AND THEN
THE INDIANS TAUGHT
THE PILGRIMS

135
00:05:29,121 --> 00:05:30,789
WHAT IT MEANT TO BE HOT
IN THE NEW WORLD.

136
00:05:32,332 --> 00:05:34,375
HI.
HELLO, EVERYBODY.

137
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:35,627
HI.

138
00:05:35,627 --> 00:05:38,421
HI, DAD. MOM.

139
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,841
LOOK... LOOK WHO IT IS.

140
00:05:40,841 --> 00:05:42,634
IT'S CHANDLER.

141
00:05:42,634 --> 00:05:44,261
OH, YES, OF COURSE.

142
00:05:44,261 --> 00:05:46,554
HELLO, CHANDLER.

143
00:05:46,554 --> 00:05:47,931
MR. AND MRS. GELLER,
YOU LOOK WONDERFUL.

144
00:05:47,931 --> 00:05:50,851
IT IS GREAT TO
HAVE YOU HERE.

145
00:05:50,851 --> 00:05:52,351
LET US TAKE
OFF YOUR COATS.

146
00:05:52,351 --> 00:05:56,190
WHOA, SNOWING OUT THERE?

147
00:05:56,190 --> 00:05:57,398
NO.

148
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:06,658
MONICA, ALL THIS FOOD
LOOKS WONDERFUL.

149
00:06:06,658 --> 00:06:08,618
YOU SHOULD THINK
ABOUT DOING THIS
FOR A LIVING.

150
00:06:11,663 --> 00:06:14,082
OKAY. I HAVE DANDRUFF.

151
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:16,251
THERE'S NO NEED
TO LAUGH AND POINT.

152
00:06:16,251 --> 00:06:19,963
DAD, CHANDLER WAS JUST LAUGHING
AT YOUR JOKE.

153
00:06:19,963 --> 00:06:21,715
MY JOKE WASN'T FUNNY.

154
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:25,468
RACH, RACH...
YEAH.

155
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:28,889
I JUST REMEMBERED.
I HAD A DREAM ABOUT
MR. GELLER LAST NIGHT.

156
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:30,682
REALLY?
YEAH.

157
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:32,851
I DREAMT THAT HE
SAVED ME FROM A
BURNING BUILDING

158
00:06:32,851 --> 00:06:35,270
AND HE WAS SO BRAVE
AND SO STRONG

159
00:06:35,270 --> 00:06:38,523
AND IT'S MAKING ME
LOOK AT HIM
TOTALLY DIFFERENTLY.

160
00:06:39,691 --> 00:06:41,026
YOU KNOW?

161
00:06:41,026 --> 00:06:42,443
I MEAN, HE USED TO
BE JUST, YOU KNOW

162
00:06:42,443 --> 00:06:44,154
JACK GELLER, MONICA
AND ROSS'S DAD

163
00:06:44,154 --> 00:06:47,032
AND NOW HE'S
JACK GELLER,
DREAM HUNK.

164
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:51,745
Rachel:
I DON'T KNOW.

165
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:53,914
YOU KNOW, TO ME,
HE'LL ALWAYS BE
JACK GELLER--

166
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:55,498
WALKS IN WHILE
YOU'RE CHANGING.

167
00:06:59,753 --> 00:07:01,255
YOU KNOW, DAD,
CHANDLER IS ONE

168
00:07:01,255 --> 00:07:03,422
OF ROSS'S VERY
BEST FRIENDS.

169
00:07:03,422 --> 00:07:05,592
YOU KNOW,
ROSS SURE IS A GREAT GUY.

170
00:07:05,592 --> 00:07:07,261
YOU KNOW, I'VE ALWAYS FELT

171
00:07:07,261 --> 00:07:10,638
THAT HOW A YOUNG MAN TURNS OUT
IS A REFLECTION ON HIS FATHER.

172
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:12,431
I ALWAYS THOUGHT THAT, TOO.

173
00:07:12,431 --> 00:07:14,393
TELL ME,
WHAT DOES YOUR FATHER DO?

174
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,688
HE'S A HEADLINER OF A...

175
00:07:18,688 --> 00:07:21,316
GAY BURLESQUE SHOW.

176
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:24,819
RACH, YOU'RE KILLING US HERE.

177
00:07:24,819 --> 00:07:26,696
WILL YOU SERVE
THE DESSERT ALREADY?

178
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:29,699
THERE'S DRUNKEN
DANCERS AWAITING.

179
00:07:29,699 --> 00:07:31,492
WELL, LOOK AT IT.
ISN'T IT BEAUTIFUL?

180
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:32,911
YEAH, YEAH,
WHAT IS IT?

181
00:07:32,911 --> 00:07:34,288
IT'S A TRIFLE

182
00:07:34,288 --> 00:07:36,164
AND IT'S GOT ALL
OF THESE LAYERS.

183
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:38,292
FIRST, THERE'S A LAYER
OF LADYFINGERS

184
00:07:38,292 --> 00:07:39,793
THEN A LAYER OF JAM

185
00:07:39,793 --> 00:07:42,087
THEN CUSTARD,
WHICH I MADE FROM SCRATCH.

186
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:43,213
THEN RASPBERRIES

187
00:07:43,213 --> 00:07:44,714
MORE LADYFINGERS

188
00:07:44,714 --> 00:07:47,592
THEN BEEF SAUTEED
WITH PEAS AND ONIONS

189
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:51,054
AND THEN A LITTLE
BIT MORE CUSTARD,
AND THEN BANANAS

190
00:07:51,054 --> 00:07:53,974
AND THEN I JUST PUT
SOME WHIPPED CREAM ON TOP.

191
00:07:57,685 --> 00:08:00,939
WHAT WAS THE ONE
RIGHT BEFORE BANANAS?

192
00:08:02,941 --> 00:08:08,238
THE BEEF? YEAH, THAT
WAS WEIRD TO ME, TOO,
BUT, THEN, YOU KNOW

193
00:08:08,238 --> 00:08:10,407
I THOUGHT, WELL,
THERE'S MINCEMEAT PIE.

194
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:11,408
I MEAN, THAT'S AN
ENGLISH DESSERT.

195
00:08:11,408 --> 00:08:12,742
THESE PEOPLE JUST PUT

196
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:16,121
VERY STRANGE THINGS
IN THEIR FOOD, YOU KNOW?

197
00:08:16,121 --> 00:08:17,747
OH, BY THE WAY, CAN I BORROW
SOME RUM FROM YOUR PLACE?

198
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:19,458
YEAH, SURE, YEAH.

199
00:08:19,458 --> 00:08:21,501
AND WHILE I'M GONE,
DON'T YOU BOYS SNEAK A TASTE.

200
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:23,837
RIGHT.
OKAY.

201
00:08:25,797 --> 00:08:27,841
BEEF IN A DESSERT?

202
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:30,802
THERE... NO, NO, NO.
THERE IS NO WAY.

203
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:34,389
I KNOW, AND ONLY
ONE LAYER OF JAM?

204
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:39,936
WHAT IS UP WITH THAT?

205
00:08:39,936 --> 00:08:41,480
OH, MY GOD.

206
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:44,983
THE PAGES ARE STUCK TOGETHER.

207
00:08:44,983 --> 00:08:45,984
CHANDLER!

208
00:08:52,407 --> 00:08:54,034
OH, MY GOD.

209
00:08:54,034 --> 00:08:57,996
SHE... SHE MADE HALF
AN ENGLISH TRIFLE AND...

210
00:08:57,996 --> 00:09:02,083
HALF A SHEPHERD'S PIE.

211
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:03,543
OH, MAN.

212
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,295
NOW SHE'S GOING
TO START ALL OVER.

213
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:06,713
WE'RE NEVER GOING
TO GET TO INTRODUCE

214
00:09:06,713 --> 00:09:09,549
THE HOT GIRLS
TO THE NEW WORLD.

215
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,009
NO, NO, WE WILL.

216
00:09:11,009 --> 00:09:12,886
WE JUST WON'T TELL HER
SHE MESSED UP.

217
00:09:12,886 --> 00:09:15,055
JUST LET HER SERVE
THE BEEF CUSTARD THING?

218
00:09:15,055 --> 00:09:16,555
YEAH.

219
00:09:16,555 --> 00:09:19,100
IT WILL BE LIKE A FUNNY
THANKSGIVING STORY.

220
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,145
VOMITING STORIES
ARE FUNNY, I GUESS.

221
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:26,316
JOEY, GOD, YOUR APARTMENT
IS, LIKE, A HUNDRED DEGREES.

222
00:09:26,316 --> 00:09:29,069
DID IT MAKE YOU WANT
TO WALK AROUND IN
YOUR UNDERWEAR?

223
00:09:29,069 --> 00:09:30,904
NO.

224
00:09:30,904 --> 00:09:33,281
STILL NOT HOT ENOUGH.

225
00:09:36,368 --> 00:09:37,702
YEAH.
RACHEL.

226
00:09:37,702 --> 00:09:39,454
OKAY. LOOK AT HIM.

227
00:09:39,454 --> 00:09:41,664
LOOK AT THOSE
STRONG HANDS.

228
00:09:41,664 --> 00:09:45,835
OH, WHAT I WOULDN'T
GIVE TO BE THAT CAN
OF CONDENSED MILK.

229
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:51,383
MOM, CHANDLER
WAS JUST SAYING

230
00:09:51,383 --> 00:09:53,260
HOW BEAUTIFUL
YOUR SWEATER IS.

231
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:55,220
OH, THANK YOU, CHANDLER.
I JUST BOUGHT IT.

232
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:57,556
OH, YES. WELL,
IT'S VERY BEAUTIFUL.

233
00:09:57,556 --> 00:09:59,891
IT'S CREAM-COLORED
AND TIGHT, AND...

234
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:03,520
I DON'T MEAN TIGHT.

235
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:04,812
IT'S NOT TOO TIGHT.

236
00:10:04,812 --> 00:10:06,398
NOT THAT I WAS LOOKING AT...

237
00:10:06,398 --> 00:10:08,691
WHAT'S THE MATTER
WITH HIM?

238
00:10:08,691 --> 00:10:11,528
I THINK HE'S STONED AGAIN.

239
00:10:11,528 --> 00:10:12,695
WHAT?

240
00:10:12,695 --> 00:10:13,905
WHAT?

241
00:10:13,905 --> 00:10:15,532
DUDE, I NEED TO TALK TO YOU
A SEC.

242
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:22,622
OKAY.

243
00:10:22,622 --> 00:10:25,417
I THINK I MIGHT KNOW WHY
MY PARENTS DON'T LIKE YOU.

244
00:10:25,417 --> 00:10:26,667
YOU DO? WHY?

245
00:10:26,667 --> 00:10:28,462
OKAY, REMEMBER--
WE WERE YOUNG...

246
00:10:28,462 --> 00:10:31,506
SPRING BREAK,
SOPHOMORE YEAR.

247
00:10:31,506 --> 00:10:33,592
I GOT HIGH
IN MY BEDROOM

248
00:10:33,592 --> 00:10:35,093
AND MY PARENTS WALKED IN
AND SMELLED IT

249
00:10:35,093 --> 00:10:36,761
AND SO I TOLD THEM

250
00:10:36,761 --> 00:10:39,514
THAT YOU HAD GOTTEN STONED
AND JUMPED OUT THE WINDOW.

251
00:10:41,099 --> 00:10:42,809
WHAT?
WHY DID YOU DO THAT?

252
00:10:42,809 --> 00:10:44,436
I DON'T KNOW.

253
00:10:44,436 --> 00:10:46,938
YOURS WAS THE FIRST NAME
THAT POPPED INTO MY HEAD.

254
00:10:46,938 --> 00:10:49,274
I'M SORRY.
I DIDN'T THINK IT WOULD MATTER.

255
00:10:49,274 --> 00:10:50,525
HOW COULD IT NOT MATTER?

256
00:10:50,525 --> 00:10:52,026
WELL, HOW WAS I
SUPPOSED TO KNOW

257
00:10:52,026 --> 00:10:53,612
WE'D END UP BEING
FRIENDS AFTER COLLEGE

258
00:10:53,612 --> 00:10:55,530
LET ALONE YOU'D BE
LIVING WITH MY SISTER?

259
00:10:55,530 --> 00:10:57,532
WHAT ABOUT ALL THAT
"FRIENDS FOREVER" STUFF?

260
00:10:57,532 --> 00:10:58,825
I DON'T KNOW.

261
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:00,327
I WAS ALL HIGH.

262
00:11:06,291 --> 00:11:08,627
MOM AND DAD JUST SENT ME
IN HERE TO FIND OUT

263
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:10,670
IF YOU WERE TRYING
TO GET ROSS STONED.

264
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:15,634
YOUR PARENTS CAUGHT ROSS
SMOKING POT IN COLLEGE

265
00:11:15,634 --> 00:11:16,968
AND HE BLAMED IT ON ME.

266
00:11:16,968 --> 00:11:18,845
ROSS, I CAN'T BELIEVE
YOU'D DO THAT.

267
00:11:18,845 --> 00:11:21,348
THE REASON WE HAVEN'T
TOLD THEM WE'RE TOGETHER

268
00:11:21,348 --> 00:11:22,681
IS BECAUSE THEY HATE ME.

269
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:24,017
OKAY? SO, WILL
YOU FIX THIS?

270
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,560
OKAY. OKAY.

271
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:28,271
I'LL TELL THEM
IT WASN'T CHANDLER WHO GOT HIGH.

272
00:11:28,271 --> 00:11:30,064
NOW, WHO SHOULD I SAY IT WAS?

273
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:32,400
YOU!

274
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:34,402
IT'S NOT LIKE
IT WAS A BIG DEAL.

275
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:36,613
YOU DON'T STILL
DO IT OR ANYTHING.

276
00:11:36,613 --> 00:11:38,156
ALL RIGHT, ALL RIGHT.

277
00:11:38,156 --> 00:11:40,659
NOW, WHO SHOULD I SAY
"TRICKED" ME INTO DOING IT?

278
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:47,748
DAD.

279
00:11:47,748 --> 00:11:49,459
DAD, PLEASE DON'T
PICK YOUR TEETH OUT HERE.

280
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:52,337
ALL RIGHT, AND IF YOU'RE
GOING TO PUT YOUR FEET UP...

281
00:11:52,337 --> 00:11:54,005
MONICA, LEAVE HIM ALONE!

282
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,676
WILL YOU HURRY UP!

283
00:11:57,676 --> 00:11:59,553
DID YOU NOT
HEAR ME BEFORE

284
00:11:59,553 --> 00:12:02,013
WHEN I TOLD YOU THAT
ALL OF JANINE'S FRIENDS
ARE DANCERS, HUH?

285
00:12:02,013 --> 00:12:05,392
AND THAT THEY'RE GOING
TO BE DRINKING A LOT?

286
00:12:05,392 --> 00:12:09,646
NO, I DID, BUT TELL ME AGAIN
'CAUSE IT'S SO ROMANTIC.

287
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:12,065
YOU'RE WHIPPING SO SLOW.
CAN'T YOU DO IT ANY FASTER?

288
00:12:12,065 --> 00:12:14,859
JOEY, COME ON.
I DON'T WANT TO MAKE
ANY MISTAKES, ALL RIGHT?

289
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:16,944
THIS IS THE ONLY DESSERT
AND IF I SCREW IT UP

290
00:12:16,944 --> 00:12:18,238
EVERYBODY'S GOING
TO BE, LIKE

291
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:19,698
"OH, REMEMBER
THAT THANKSGIVING

292
00:12:19,698 --> 00:12:21,366
WHEN RACHEL SCREWED
UP THE TRIFLE?"

293
00:12:21,366 --> 00:12:24,118
OKAY?

294
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,538
SO WHY DON'T YOU JUST
LET ME WORRY ABOUT
MAKING THE TRIFLE

295
00:12:26,538 --> 00:12:28,248
AND YOU JUST WORRY
ABOUT EATING IT,
ALL RIGHT?

296
00:12:28,248 --> 00:12:31,167
OH, I AM.

297
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,420
ROSS, IF YOU
DON'T TELL THEM,
THEN I WILL.

298
00:12:33,420 --> 00:12:35,505
OKAY, FINE.

299
00:12:35,505 --> 00:12:37,924
ROSS, CAN I TALK
TO YOU FOR A SECOND?

300
00:12:37,924 --> 00:12:40,093
OH, UH, CAN'T IT
WAIT A SECOND, JOEY?

301
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:42,220
I HAVE TO TELL MY
PARENTS SOMETHING.

302
00:12:42,220 --> 00:12:43,513
NO, IT CAN'T?
OKAY.

303
00:12:47,225 --> 00:12:50,811
OKAY, LOOK, I THINK
WE HAVE TO TELL RACHEL

304
00:12:50,811 --> 00:12:52,021
SHE MESSED UP HER DESSERT.

305
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:54,232
WHAT? WHAT IS
WITH EVERYBODY?

306
00:12:54,232 --> 00:12:58,903
IT'S THANKSGIVING,
NOT TRUTH DAY.

307
00:12:58,903 --> 00:13:03,032
LOOK, WHEN EVERYONE EATS
THAT BANANA MEAT THING

308
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:04,033
THEY'RE ALL GOING
TO MAKE FUN OF HER.

309
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:05,826
DO YOU WANT THAT?

310
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:07,537
OKAY, OKAY, WE'LL
JUST GET EVERYONE

311
00:13:07,537 --> 00:13:09,372
TO ACT LIKE
THEY LIKE IT.

312
00:13:09,372 --> 00:13:11,458
THAT WAY, NO ONE
MAKES FUN OF HER

313
00:13:11,458 --> 00:13:14,961
AND WE STILL GET TO GO
TO SWEET POTATO PIE.

314
00:13:14,961 --> 00:13:17,964
DUDE, THEY'RE NOT OBJECTS.

315
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:20,841
JUST KIDDING.
I'LL TALK TO THEM.

316
00:13:20,841 --> 00:13:23,886
YOU DISTRACT HER.

317
00:13:23,886 --> 00:13:26,931
HEY, RACH, CAN I TALK
TO YOU OUTSIDE FOR A SEC?

318
00:13:29,016 --> 00:13:30,685
OKAY.

319
00:13:36,441 --> 00:13:39,026
WHAT'S UP, ROSS?

320
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:41,446
SO, UM...

321
00:13:41,446 --> 00:13:44,031
THANKSGIVING.

322
00:13:44,031 --> 00:13:48,953
THE HOLIDAY SEASON
IS UPON US, HMM?

323
00:13:50,079 --> 00:13:51,539
YEAH.

324
00:13:51,539 --> 00:13:57,044
AND, UM, YOU
LOOK NICE TODAY.

325
00:13:57,044 --> 00:13:58,171
OH, NO.

326
00:13:58,171 --> 00:13:59,714
NO, ROSS. DON'T DO THIS.

327
00:13:59,714 --> 00:14:00,715
WHAT?

328
00:14:00,715 --> 00:14:02,175
I JUST... I DON'T THINK

329
00:14:02,175 --> 00:14:05,094
US GETTING BACK TOGETHER
IS A GOOD IDEA.

330
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,722
HUH?

331
00:14:07,722 --> 00:14:10,809
I THOUGHT THIS MIGHT
HAPPEN TODAY. ROSS...

332
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:13,269
I KNOW THE HOLIDAYS
CAN BE ROUGH, YOU KNOW?

333
00:14:13,269 --> 00:14:16,606
AND IT'S PROBABLY REALLY HARD
FOR YOU TO BE ALONE RIGHT NOW.

334
00:14:16,606 --> 00:14:17,940
YOU'RE ALONE.

335
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:20,443
NO, I-I LIVE
WITH PHOEBE.

336
00:14:20,443 --> 00:14:24,322
I MEAN, YOU'RE
ALONE ALONE.

337
00:14:24,322 --> 00:14:25,699
YOU KNOW?
AND I JUST...

338
00:14:25,699 --> 00:14:27,617
IT'S JUST NOT
THE TIME FOR US.

339
00:14:27,617 --> 00:14:29,285
I'M SORRY.

340
00:14:29,285 --> 00:14:32,413
OH, WELL. CAN'T BLAME
A GUY FOR TRYING.

341
00:14:34,040 --> 00:14:35,124
SO...

342
00:14:35,124 --> 00:14:36,125
( stutters )

343
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:37,126
OKAY...

344
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,712
AND, UH, IF ANYONE
NEEDS HELP

345
00:14:38,712 --> 00:14:39,920
PRETENDING
TO LIKE IT

346
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:41,922
I LEARNED SOME THINGS
IN ACTING CLASS.

347
00:14:41,922 --> 00:14:44,425
TRY RUBBING YOUR STOMACH.

348
00:14:44,425 --> 00:14:45,635
OR, UH...

349
00:14:45,635 --> 00:14:47,970
OR SAYING "MMM."

350
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:50,598
AND, UH, OOH, OHH-- SMILING.

351
00:14:50,598 --> 00:14:52,308
OKAY.

352
00:14:52,308 --> 00:14:54,894
I'M NOT GOING TO PAY FOR
THOSE ACTING CLASSES ANYMORE.

353
00:14:56,563 --> 00:14:59,232
Joey:
RACHEL, THERE
YOU ARE.

354
00:14:59,232 --> 00:15:01,234
COME ON. LET'S SERVE
THAT DESSERT ALREADY.

355
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:03,528
JOEY, YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE TO STOP RUSHING ME.

356
00:15:03,528 --> 00:15:05,572
YOU KNOW WHAT?
YOU DON'T GET ANY DESSERT.

357
00:15:05,572 --> 00:15:07,407
REALLY?

358
00:15:07,407 --> 00:15:08,658
NO, I'M JUST KIDDING.

359
00:15:08,658 --> 00:15:11,494
I WOULD NEVER
DO THAT TO YOU.

360
00:15:11,494 --> 00:15:13,872
OKAY, EVERYBODY,
IT'S TRIFLE TIME.

361
00:15:13,872 --> 00:15:15,707
SO, NOW, RACH...

362
00:15:15,707 --> 00:15:18,292
THIS IS A TRADITIONAL
ENGLISH TRIFLE, ISN'T IT?

363
00:15:18,292 --> 00:15:19,794
IT SURE IS.

364
00:15:19,794 --> 00:15:22,088
WOW. SO, THEN, DID YOU MAKE IT
WITH BEEF OR EGGPLANT?

365
00:15:22,088 --> 00:15:23,172
BEEF.

366
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,632
I CAN'T HAVE ANY, YOU KNOW?

367
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:25,925
I DON'T EAT BEEF.

368
00:15:25,925 --> 00:15:29,053
( all groaning and sighing )

369
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:30,346
ALL RIGHT, MONICA

370
00:15:30,346 --> 00:15:32,724
I WANT YOU TO HAVE
THE FIRST TASTE.

371
00:15:32,724 --> 00:15:34,141
REALLY?

372
00:15:36,811 --> 00:15:38,479
OH, WAIT-WAIT!

373
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,647
YOU ONLY GOT WHIPPED CREAM
IN THERE.

374
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:40,648
YOU'VE GOT TO TAKE A BITE

375
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:43,359
WITH ALL
THE LAYERS.

376
00:15:43,359 --> 00:15:45,152
OKAY.

377
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:47,655
OOPS, YOU DROPPED A PEA.

378
00:15:57,373 --> 00:15:58,625
WELL?

379
00:15:58,625 --> 00:16:02,295
MMM...

380
00:16:07,341 --> 00:16:09,928
IT'S GOOD.

381
00:16:09,928 --> 00:16:11,888
REALLY? HOW GOOD?

382
00:16:11,888 --> 00:16:14,140
IT'S SO GOOD THAT I
FEEL REALLY SELFISH

383
00:16:14,140 --> 00:16:16,183
BEING THE ONLY ONE
WHO'S EATING IT.

384
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:19,479
AND I THINK WE SHOULD
HAVE EVERYONE TASTE
HOW GOOD IT IS.

385
00:16:19,479 --> 00:16:21,564
ESPECIALLY ROSS.

386
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:26,986
MM-HMM.

387
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:28,696
All:
MMM...

388
00:16:28,696 --> 00:16:30,323
YEAH, THIS IS SO GOOD

389
00:16:30,323 --> 00:16:32,951
THAT I'M GOING TO GO
ENJOY IT ON THE BALCONY.

390
00:16:34,828 --> 00:16:39,081
SO I CAN ENJOY THE VIEW
WHILST I ENJOY MY DESSERT.

391
00:16:40,583 --> 00:16:42,710
AND I'M GOING TO CALL
MY FRIEND, MARY

392
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:45,630
AND TELL HER HOW GOOD
THIS IS FROM MONICA'S ROOM.

393
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:46,673
I'LL HELP YOU DIAL.

394
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:51,260
AND I'M GOING TO GO
INTO THE BATHROOM

395
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:54,347
SO I CAN LOOK AT IT
IN THE MIRROR AS I EAT IT.

396
00:16:55,682 --> 00:16:57,642
OKAY, NOW, WHAT WAS THAT
ALL ABOUT?

397
00:16:57,642 --> 00:16:59,477
IS IT...
DOES IT NOT TASTE GOOD?

398
00:16:59,477 --> 00:17:00,561
LET ME TRY THAT.

399
00:17:00,561 --> 00:17:01,813
NO! NO!

400
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,986
ALL GONE.

401
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:12,031
SO GOOD.

402
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:15,075
MAYBE CHANDLER
HAS SOME LEFT.

403
00:17:17,537 --> 00:17:19,622
IT TASTES LIKE FEET.

404
00:17:21,833 --> 00:17:23,584
I LIKE IT.

405
00:17:27,213 --> 00:17:28,798
ARE YOU KIDDING?

406
00:17:28,798 --> 00:17:29,966
WHAT'S NOT TO LIKE?

407
00:17:29,966 --> 00:17:31,217
CUSTARD? GOOD.

408
00:17:31,217 --> 00:17:32,677
JAM? GOOD.

409
00:17:32,677 --> 00:17:34,929
MEAT? GOOD!

410
00:17:37,390 --> 00:17:40,601
SO A BIRD JUST GRABBED IT
AND THEN...

411
00:17:43,229 --> 00:17:46,065
AND THEN TRIED
TO FLY AWAY WITH IT AND...

412
00:17:46,065 --> 00:17:49,151
AND THEN JUST DROPPED IT
ON THE STREET?

413
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:52,488
YES, BUT IF IT'S
ANY CONSOLATION

414
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:55,533
BEFORE THE BIRD DROPPED IT,
HE SEEMED TO ENJOY IT.

415
00:17:57,744 --> 00:17:59,537
RACHEL, COME HERE.

416
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:00,955
OKAY...

417
00:18:00,955 --> 00:18:03,081
I WAS JUST STARTING
TO TAKE MY THANKSGIVING NAP

418
00:18:03,081 --> 00:18:04,709
AND I HAD ANOTHER
DREAM ABOUT JACK.

419
00:18:04,709 --> 00:18:06,002
UH, PHOEBE, DO I
WANT TO HEAR THIS?

420
00:18:06,002 --> 00:18:07,378
I DON'T KNOW.
LET'S SEE.

421
00:18:07,378 --> 00:18:08,629
SO... OKAY, I DREAMT

422
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,339
THAT WE WERE GOING
TO GET MARRIED

423
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:12,884
AND HE LEFT BECAUSE
HE HAD TO GO FIGHT A FIRE.

424
00:18:12,884 --> 00:18:15,094
AND, UM, SO, OKAY,
I WENT TO A NIGHTCLUB

425
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,179
AND I SAW HIM MAKING OUT
WITH A GIRL.

426
00:18:17,179 --> 00:18:18,222
OH, MY GOD.

427
00:18:18,222 --> 00:18:21,308
HE DREAM-CHEATED ON YOU.

428
00:18:21,308 --> 00:18:23,686
YEAH. BUT THEN
JACQUES COUSTEAU CAME

429
00:18:23,686 --> 00:18:25,855
AND HE KICKED HIS ASS
FOR BETRAYING ME.

430
00:18:25,855 --> 00:18:27,982
HE WAS SO COOL.

431
00:18:27,982 --> 00:18:29,943
AND THEN, HE
TOOK ME DIVING

432
00:18:29,943 --> 00:18:31,652
AND HE INTRODUCED ME
TO HIS PET SEA HORSE

433
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:33,529
WHO, BY THE WAY, WAS
TOTALLY COMING ON TO ME

434
00:18:33,529 --> 00:18:35,073
AND PLEASE, THAT IS
NOT GOING TO HAPPEN.

435
00:18:37,909 --> 00:18:42,120
BOY, I'M GLAD I WORE
THE BIG BELT TODAY.

436
00:18:42,120 --> 00:18:44,040
WOW.

437
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,834
FIVE MINUTES AGO,
A LINE LIKE THAT
WOULD HAVE FLOORED ME.

438
00:18:48,086 --> 00:18:50,129
NOW NOTHING.
WELL, NOT NOTHING.

439
00:18:50,129 --> 00:18:51,798
I AM STILL A WOMAN.

440
00:18:54,634 --> 00:18:55,843
ROSS...

441
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:57,177
LET'S GO.

442
00:18:57,177 --> 00:18:59,513
OH, YEAH, ABOUT TELLING
MOM AND DAD

443
00:18:59,513 --> 00:19:02,850
I WAS THINKING ABOUT
MAYBE WRITING A LETTER.

444
00:19:02,850 --> 00:19:04,060
YOU KNOW WHAT?
THAT'S IT.

445
00:19:04,060 --> 00:19:05,227
YOU'VE HAD YOUR CHANCE.

446
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:10,691
MOM, DAD, ROSS
SMOKED POT IN COLLEGE.

447
00:19:10,691 --> 00:19:11,692
WHAT?
WHAT?

448
00:19:11,692 --> 00:19:15,154
YOU ARE SUCH A TATTLETALE!

449
00:19:17,865 --> 00:19:19,951
MOM, DAD...

450
00:19:19,951 --> 00:19:21,494
YOU REMEMBER THAT...

451
00:19:21,494 --> 00:19:25,790
THAT TIME YOU WALKED IN MY ROOM
AND SMELLED MARIJUANA?

452
00:19:25,790 --> 00:19:26,874
YES.
YES.

453
00:19:30,544 --> 00:19:33,380
WELL, I TOLD YOU IT WAS CHANDLER

454
00:19:33,380 --> 00:19:38,136
WHO WAS SMOKING THE POT, BUT...

455
00:19:38,136 --> 00:19:39,386
IT WAS ME.

456
00:19:39,386 --> 00:19:41,263
I'M SORRY.

457
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,765
IT WAS YOU?

458
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:44,142
Monica:
AND DAD

459
00:19:44,142 --> 00:19:46,019
YOU KNOW THAT MAILMAN
THAT YOU GOT FIRED?

460
00:19:46,019 --> 00:19:47,645
HE DIDN'T STEAL YOUR PLAYBOYS.

461
00:19:47,645 --> 00:19:48,729
ROSS DID.

462
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:50,481
OH...

463
00:19:53,526 --> 00:19:56,988
YEAH, WELL, HURRICANE GLORIA
DIDN'T BREAK THE PORCH SWING.

464
00:19:56,988 --> 00:19:58,280
MONICA DID!

465
00:20:00,741 --> 00:20:03,619
ROSS HASN'T WORKED
AT THE MUSEUM FOR A YEAR!

466
00:20:05,079 --> 00:20:07,040
MONICA AND CHANDLER
ARE LIVING TOGETHER!

467
00:20:10,668 --> 00:20:14,881
ROSS MARRIED RACHEL IN VEGAS
AND GOT DIVORCED AGAIN!

468
00:20:16,423 --> 00:20:18,718
I LOVE JACQUES COUSTEAU!

469
00:20:21,261 --> 00:20:24,932
I WASN'T SUPPOSED
TO PUT BEEF IN THE TRIFLE!

470
00:20:24,932 --> 00:20:28,394
I WANT TO GO!

471
00:20:30,771 --> 00:20:35,776
THAT'S A LOT OF INFORMATION
TO GET IN 30 SECONDS.

472
00:20:35,776 --> 00:20:37,737
ALL RIGHT

473
00:20:37,737 --> 00:20:39,864
JOEY, IF YOU WANT
TO LEAVE, JUST LEAVE.

474
00:20:41,699 --> 00:20:45,161
RACHEL, NO, YOU WEREN'T
SUPPOSED TO PUT BEEF
IN THE TRIFLE.

475
00:20:45,161 --> 00:20:48,330
IT DID NOT TASTE GOOD.

476
00:20:50,708 --> 00:20:55,379
PHOEBE, I'M SORRY, BUT I THINK
JACQUES COUSTEAU IS DEAD.

477
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:58,382
MONICA...

478
00:20:58,382 --> 00:20:59,508
WHY YOU FELT

479
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,052
YOU HAD TO
HIDE THE FACT

480
00:21:01,052 --> 00:21:04,055
THAT YOU ARE IN AN IMPORTANT
RELATIONSHIP IS BEYOND ME.

481
00:21:04,055 --> 00:21:07,141
AND WE KIND OF FIGURED
ABOUT THE PORCH SWING.

482
00:21:08,517 --> 00:21:10,352
ROSS...

483
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:13,814
DRUGS, DIVORCED... AGAIN.

484
00:21:15,149 --> 00:21:16,817
WHAT HAPPENED, SON?

485
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:21,572
I... I, UH, I GOT TRICKED
INTO ALL THOSE THINGS.

486
00:21:23,490 --> 00:21:27,745
CHANDLER, YOU'VE BEEN
ROSS'S BEST FRIEND
ALL THESE YEARS

487
00:21:27,745 --> 00:21:31,207
STUCK BY HIM
DURING THE DRUG PROBLEMS.

488
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:36,754
AND NOW YOU'VE
TAKEN ON MONICA AS WELL.

489
00:21:36,754 --> 00:21:39,090
WELL, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT TO SAY.

490
00:21:39,090 --> 00:21:41,884
YOU'RE A WONDERFUL
HUMAN BEING.

491
00:21:44,011 --> 00:21:45,429
THANK YOU.

492
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:46,597
NO!

493
00:21:46,597 --> 00:21:48,641
THANK YOU.

494
00:21:48,641 --> 00:21:50,434
AND MONICA AND ROSS

495
00:21:50,434 --> 00:21:53,729
I DON'T KNOW WHAT I'M GOING
TO DO ABOUT THE TWO OF YOU.

496
00:21:55,106 --> 00:21:56,857
I'LL TALK TO THEM.

497
00:22:03,363 --> 00:22:04,991
YOU GUYS,
IT WAS BANANAS

498
00:22:04,991 --> 00:22:06,617
CREAM AND BEEF.

499
00:22:06,617 --> 00:22:09,954
I JUST CANNOT BELIEVE
THAT YOU ATE THAT

500
00:22:09,954 --> 00:22:12,706
SO THAT I WOULDN'T FEEL BAD.

501
00:22:12,706 --> 00:22:14,500
ACTUALLY, I
DIDN'T EAT MINE.

502
00:22:14,500 --> 00:22:16,210
IT'S STILL IN
THE BATHROOM.

503
00:22:16,210 --> 00:22:17,295
NO, IT ISN'T.
I ATE THAT.

504
00:22:19,672 --> 00:22:22,300
AND WE LEFT OURS
IN MONICA'S BEDROOM.

505
00:22:22,300 --> 00:22:24,677
NO. GOT IT
AND GOT YOURS, TOO.

